drm/amd/display: give a DP-to-HDMI PCON its VRR range from the HF-VSDB

RC-only carry, generated against cachyos-7.3-rc3-4.

A CH7218 adapter that gets VRR on linux-cachyos-bc250 (7.2) still shows
vrr_capable=0 and a 0/0 vrr_range on linux-cachyos-rc-bc250 with the
allowlist entry in place, on a TV whose EDID carries both HDMI Forum VRR
48-120 and AMD FreeSync 48-120. The three DPCD gates in
dm_get_adaptive_sync_support_type() -- Adaptive-Sync SDP support
(0x2214 bit 0), Ignore-MSA (0x007 bit 6) and the allowlist -- all pass
on this adapter (read back: 0x15, 0xc1, OUI 2B02F0), so the connector
does reach the FREESYNC_TYPE_PCON_IN_WHITELIST block.

That block takes its range only from the AMD VSDB, and only through
parse_hdmi_amd_vsdb(), which hands the CEA block to DMUB or DMCU
firmware. DCN201 has neither: dm_dmub_sw_init() has no case for it and
dcn201_resource sets disable_dmcu, so dc_edid_parser_send_cea() returns
false and the parse fails with -ENODEV on every Cyan Skillfish. Nothing
sets a range, freesync_capable stays false. The 7.2 series works because
CachyOS's 7.2/hdmi branch prefers the HDMI 2.1 VRR range the DRM core
parses in software from the HF-VSDB; the 7.3 branch only does that on
the native HDMI path, not for a PCON.

So do the same in the PCON block: when the AMD VSDB path produced no
range and the sink advertises HF-VSDB VRR, take vrr_min/vrr_max from
there (VRRMAX = 0 meaning "up to the base refresh rate", resolved the
way the HDMI branch does), set pack_sdp_v1_3 and the adaptive-sync
type, and publish the range. The DPCD gates are untouched, and a sink
with a usable AMD VSDB still takes that path first. Also covers TVs with
no AMD VSDB at all -- an LG G5 has only the HDMI and HF-VSDB blocks.

Logs "VRR: PCON HF-VSDB fallback: ..." at drm_dbg_driver level next to
the existing "VRR:" lines, so drm.debug=0x2 shows the decision.

---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index 955c70e..7b16f60 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -4020,6 +4020,57 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps(struct drm_connector *connector,
 				connector->display_info.monitor_range.max_vfreq = vsdb_info.max_refresh_rate_hz;
 			}
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * The AMD VSDB above is parsed by DMUB or DMCU firmware. DCN201
+		 * (Cyan Skillfish) has neither -- no dmub_srv, disable_dmcu --
+		 * so parse_hdmi_amd_vsdb() always fails there and a DP-to-HDMI
+		 * PCON never gets a VRR range, even though the DPCD gates
+		 * (Adaptive-Sync SDP, Ignore-MSA, allowlist) all passed. Many TVs
+		 * also carry no AMD VSDB at all. In both cases the HDMI 2.1 VRR
+		 * range from the HF-VSDB, parsed in software by the DRM core, is
+		 * the right answer -- it is what the HDMI branch above already
+		 * falls back to, and what makes the same adapter work on 7.2.
+		 */
+		if (!freesync_capable && connector->display_info.hdmi.vrr_cap.supported) {
+			struct drm_hdmi_vrr_cap *vrr_cap =
+				&connector->display_info.hdmi.vrr_cap;
+
+			if (vrr_cap->vrr_min > 0) {
+				amdgpu_dm_connector->min_vfreq = vrr_cap->vrr_min;
+				amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq = vrr_cap->vrr_max ?
+					vrr_cap->vrr_max :
+					connector->display_info.monitor_range.max_vfreq;
+
+				/* VRRMAX = 0 means "up to the Base Refresh Rate" */
+				if (!amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq) {
+					struct drm_display_mode *brr_mode =
+						amdgpu_dm_get_highest_refresh_rate_mode(amdgpu_dm_connector, true);
+
+					if (brr_mode)
+						amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq =
+							drm_mode_vrefresh(brr_mode);
+				}
+
+				if (amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq -
+				    amdgpu_dm_connector->min_vfreq > 10) {
+					freesync_capable = true;
+					amdgpu_dm_connector->pack_sdp_v1_3 = true;
+					amdgpu_dm_connector->as_type = as_type;
+
+					connector->display_info.monitor_range.min_vfreq =
+						amdgpu_dm_connector->min_vfreq;
+					connector->display_info.monitor_range.max_vfreq =
+						amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq;
+				}
+			}
+
+			drm_dbg_driver(adev_to_drm(adev),
+				       "VRR: PCON HF-VSDB fallback: vrr_cap[min=%d max=%d] -> min=%d max=%d fs_capable=%d\n",
+				       vrr_cap->vrr_min, vrr_cap->vrr_max,
+				       amdgpu_dm_connector->min_vfreq,
+				       amdgpu_dm_connector->max_vfreq, freesync_capable);
+		}
 	}
 
 	/* Handle MCCS */
